# Unified RME workspace page sequence (permanent rules)

Applies to `RME Tulisan Tangan Lengkap` (`rme.visits.medical-record.show`) and
every surface that renders the patient's RME book.

## The product rule

1. Published legacy RME PDFs **participate directly** in the
   `RME Tulisan Tangan Lengkap` page navigation. They are not a separate
   document section, and the top document rail must never be the **only** way to
   reach them.
2. A doctor must be able to reach every legacy page using the **same**
   `Sebelumnya` / `Berikutnya` / swipe navigation used for handwritten pages.
   Requiring a scroll to Riwayat RME, or an "open PDF" step before every page,
   is a failed implementation.
3. A legacy PDF containing **N** pages contributes **N** read-only virtual
   workspace pages, unless a future explicitly approved presentation model
   supersedes this rule.
4. The global `Halaman X dari Y` counts the **unified** sequence: native
   handwriting pages plus every authorized legacy archive page.

## The persistence boundary

5. Native and legacy pages share **presentation navigation** and never share
   **persistence semantics**.
   - native page = persisted, editable native clinical sheet page
   - legacy page = immutable, read-only archive evidence
6. A legacy virtual page must **never** create a `ClinicVisit`, a
   `MedicalRecord`, a handwriting page row, or any odontogram / invoice /
   payment / `LabOrder` / SATUSEHAT record. No shadow native row may be created
   to make an archive page fit the sequence.
7. The page kind is an **explicit** field (`RmeWorkspacePage::$type`). Never
   infer it from an id range, a workspace index, a label or a URL shape.

## Read-only enforcement

8. A legacy page must expose **no** writing, drawing, erase, delete, replace,
   annotation-persistence or legacy-save operation. The editable figure is not
   rendered at all on an archive page — an inert-but-present canvas is not
   acceptable.
9. A legacy page supports zoom in / zoom out / fit / fullscreen for clinical
   reading. Zoom must never alter the source document.
10. Read-only status is conveyed in **text** ("Hanya Baca"), never by colour
    alone. Legacy page buttons carry an `L` prefix and a spoken `aria-label`.
11. `+ Tambah Halaman RM` **always** creates a native page. It must never append
    to, modify or represent legacy evidence — including when the doctor presses
    it while viewing an archive page.

## Clinical input safety

12. Switching between native and legacy pages must not silently discard unsaved
    native clinical input. Either the state survives, or the save completes, or
    the doctor is warned.
13. Touch/swipe handling must never turn a native handwritten stroke into page
    navigation. The canvas and the open editor overlay carry `data-ignore-swipe`;
    the archive viewer sets it while zoomed, because a zoomed doctor is panning.
14. There is exactly **one** page navigator and **one** swipe implementation
    (`partials/rm-page-navigator.blade.php`, `partials/rm-page-swipe-script.blade.php`).
    Extend them; never add a second navigation system.

## Authorization and privacy

15. Legacy binary data stays private and is authorized **per request**. Being
    listed in a sequence is not an authorization decision.
16. Doctor legacy access continues to require the canonical
    `DoctorPatientScopeService`, effective-practice-branch and patient scope
    rules. **Same branch alone never grants access.**
17. Only `PUBLISHED` and canonically readable legacy evidence enters the doctor
    workspace sequence.
18. The sequence builder must **delegate** to
    `LegacyRmePatientHistoryService::publishedRecordsFor()`. It must never
    re-derive publication filtering, branch filtering, doctor scope or the VOID
    policy — one definition of "which archive may this user see", not two.
19. No KTP/NIK, patient name, storage path or checksum may appear in the page
    projection or on an archive page.

## Performance

20. PDF bytes are lazy and on-demand. The workspace must never preload every
    private PDF, base64 a PDF into the page HTML, or download documents merely to
    count pages.
21. The patient's archive is resolved **once per request** and shared by the
    clinical history, the document rail and the page sequence. Rendered-page
    counts are one aggregate, never one query per document.
22. Page count comes from **actually rendered** page rows, not a declared
    `page_count`. A record with zero rendered pages contributes exactly one
    fallback page offering the inline source PDF; it is never dropped and never
    expanded into pages that could only 404.

## Unchanged foundations

23. Patient-history legacy rendering remains available and unchanged.
24. SOURCE-RM-BINDING, separation of duties, ClinicalClock, the native cutoff
    date rule and archive-only rules are unchanged.
25. Production resting state remains `CAPABILITY=OFF`, `ADMISSION=EMPTY`,
    `ACTIVE_BATCH=NONE`.
26. `ROLL-4-WAVE-3` remains **SKIPPED / NOT REQUIRED**.
27. `CURRENT_VALID_EXPECTED_FULL_SUITE_FAILURE_BASELINE = 0`.
